// Copyright (c) 2026 Roshan. All rights reserved.// Proprietary license — see LICENSE file for details.package com.roshan.persona.selfmodify/** * NOUS — Rhino sandbox resource limits (Module 15 — Self-modify). * * Defines the per-execution resource budget for a Rhino JavaScript sandbox. * The Rhino engine is configured to enforce all three limits before yielding * control back to the script — so a runaway `while(true)` loop or an * infinitely-recursive function is guaranteed to be aborted within * [maxExecutionMs] milliseconds. * * Three independent knobs: * *  - [maxExecutionMs] — wall-clock budget. Enforced via *    [org.mozilla.javascript.Context.setInstructionObserverThreshold] + *    a custom `ContextFactory.observeInstructionCount` override that *    checks `System.nanoTime()` against the start time. When exceeded, *    a `SandboxResult.Timeout` is returned. * *  - [maxMemoryMb] — JVM heap budget. Enforced by the same instruction-count *    callback — it samples `Runtime.totalMemory() - Runtime.freeMemory()` *    and aborts with `SandboxResult.MemoryLimit` if the sandbox's heap *    footprint exceeds the budget. (This is a coarse JVM-heap check, not a *    per-context allocation limit — Rhino does not expose per-context memory *    accounting. The budget applies to the entire Rhino worker thread.) * *  - [maxInstructions] — total bytecode-instruction count. Enforced by *    Rhino's built-in instruction observer — the callback receives the *    running instruction count and aborts when it exceeds this value. *    Prevents quadratic algorithms from running for hours within budget. * * Strategy §14.2 — replaces Brain's `FakeJsSandbox` (which ignored limits) * and `NoOpJsSandbox` (which always failed). * * Note: this is a Rhino-specific configuration type, distinct from Brain's * `com.roshan.persona.brain.skill.sandbox.SandboxLimits` (which is the * portable interface-level type). `RhinoJsSandbox` converts the Brain-side * limits into this Rhino-specific type internally. * * @see RhinoJsSandbox * @see <a href="docs/adr/0008-self-modifying-js-flavor-gated.md">ADR 0008</a> */data class SandboxLimits(    /** Maximum wall-clock execution time in milliseconds. Default: 5 seconds. */    val maxExecutionMs: Long = DEFAULT_MAX_EXECUTION_MS,    /** Maximum JVM heap usage in megabytes. Default: 50 MB. */    val maxMemoryMb: Int = DEFAULT_MAX_MEMORY_MB,    /** Maximum total Rhino bytecode instructions. Default: 1 million. */    val maxInstructions: Long = DEFAULT_MAX_INSTRUCTIONS,    /**     * Instruction-count check interval.     *     * Rhino's observer fires every N bytecode instructions. Lower = tighter     * timeout enforcement (but more overhead). Higher = looser (but faster).     * 10 000 is Rhino's recommended default for sandboxed execution.     */    val instructionCheckInterval: Int = DEFAULT_INSTRUCTION_CHECK_INTERVAL,) {    companion object {        /** Default wall-clock execution budget: 5 seconds. */        const val DEFAULT_MAX_EXECUTION_MS: Long = 5_000L        /** Default JVM heap budget: 50 MB. */        const val DEFAULT_MAX_MEMORY_MB: Int = 50        /** Default instruction budget: 1 million bytecode ops. */        const val DEFAULT_MAX_INSTRUCTIONS: Long = 1_000_000L        /** Default instruction-check interval (Rhino observer threshold). */        const val DEFAULT_INSTRUCTION_CHECK_INTERVAL: Int = 10_000        /**         * Default limits — used when callers don't specify custom limits.         *         * Suitable for typical self-modifying skills (text transformation,         * data parsing, simple math). Matches the defaults in Brain's         * `com.roshan.persona.brain.skill.sandbox.SandboxLimits.DEFAULT`.         */        val DEFAULT: SandboxLimits = SandboxLimits()        /**         * Strict limits — for untrusted or first-run scripts.         *         * Halves every budget. Used when executing a freshly-installed skill         * for the first time (before its behavior is validated).         */        val STRICT: SandboxLimits = SandboxLimits(            maxExecutionMs = 2_000L,            maxMemoryMb = 16,            maxInstructions = 100_000L,            instructionCheckInterval = 1_000,        )        /**         * Generous limits — for trusted, long-running scripts (e.g., data         * processing over a large input).         *         * Use sparingly — and never for skills sourced from user input or         * untrusted LLM output.         */        val GENEROUS: SandboxLimits = SandboxLimits(            maxExecutionMs = 30_000L,            maxMemoryMb = 128,            maxInstructions = 10_000_000L,            instructionCheckInterval = 50_000,        )    }}